## 8. Repository Structure

```text
network-agent/
├── Phases.md               # 4-Hour Hackathon implementation timebox
├── SETUP.md                # Environment and dependency guide
├── AI_INSTRUCTION.md       # AI reasoning & explainer contract
├── AGENTS.md               # Autonomous coding agent constraints
├── README.md               # Product overview and documentation
├── nsat/
│   ├── cli/                # Click/Typer commands & Rich UI
│   ├── core/               # Orchestrator, Discovery & Capability Registry
│   ├── analyzers/          # C++, Java, Python, JS/TS AST adapters
│   ├── scanners/           # SAST, Secrets, Dependencies, Network, Host, Container
│   ├── normalization/      # CanonicalFinding model & Noise Filter
│   ├── correlation/        # Graph Engine, Blast Radius & Risk Scoring
│   ├── remediation/        # Patch generator, Diff applier & Verifier
│   ├── ai/                 # LLM Provider abstraction (Ollama, OpenAI, Offline)
│   └── reporting/          # Terminal, JSON, Markdown, and SARIF exporters
└── tests/
    └── demo-vuln-app/      # Deterministic multi-language demo testbed
```

---

## 9. Hackathon Scope vs. Future Roadmap

### Hackathon MVP (Current Scope)
- 4-Language AST Analyzers (C++, Java, Python, JavaScript/TypeScript).
- Local & Container network binding analysis (`127.0.0.1` vs `0.0.0.0`).
- Secret, dependency, host process, and container security audits.
- Graph correlation & Post-Compromise Blast Radius calculator.
- Surgical unified diff remediation & automated re-scan verification.

### Future Roadmap
- Additional language adapters: Go, Rust, C#, Ruby, Kotlin.
- Live read-only Cloud Security Posture Management (AWS, Azure, GCP).
- IDE background extensions for VS Code and JetBrains.
- Automated API schema fuzzing (OpenAPI/Swagger integration).

---

## 10. License & Defensive Security Scope

This tool is distributed under the **MIT License**.  
**Defensive Security Notice:** NSAT is strictly engineered for defensive vulnerability assessment, internal posture auditing, and authorized remediation. Active network checks require explicit authorization (`--authorized`). NSAT does not provide exploit generation or offensive denial-of-service capabilities.
